# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run outputs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
runs/
*.db
*.sqlite3

# ...EXCEPT run provenance. A figure has to name the commit that produced it, and
# provenance that does not ship is not provenance -- a judge would see the number
# and never the pinning. These files are small, contain no run data, and are the
# only thing standing between "the lift is X" and "the lift is X, made by THIS
# code, reproducible under HEAD or not". See CLAUDE.md section 4 and INC-011.
!runs/
runs/*
!runs/*.provenance.json

# ...AND the measured run's ledger, for the same reason one step further.
# README's third claim is "every number is recomputable from this repository",
# and a judge who cloned this and ran `recoup verify-ledger` got `rows checked: 0`
# and a genesis head of 64 zeros, because the ledger the claim rests on was not
# here. An audit trail that does not ship is not an audit trail.
#
# 5.7 MB. It is the artifact every reported figure is recomputed from -- the lift,
# the completeness count, the head hash shown on camera -- and shipping it is what
# turns that claim from an assertion into something a stranger can check in one
# command. The summary rides along so the per-arm counts can be compared against
# what replay() finds, which is the INC-009 cross-check.
!runs/batch-2000.db
!runs/batch-2000.summary.json

